window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b326-224a2d3eb16c8abd.json"]={sha256:"224a2d3eb16c8abdab63a1872c963e5c10ca0fcc518e2a98cf0e74136513df37",value:{"id":"b326","title":"哥本哈根地鐵環狀線","titleEn":"Copenhagen Cityringen","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以哥本哈根環狀地鐵為背景，建立沒有一般端點折返的循環營運實驗。課程研究列車間距、局部停站延誤與車站人流如何沿環線傳遞，並連接地下施工變形、垂直交通和設備備援的驗證資料。","summaryEn":"Use Copenhagen Cityringen to construct a circular-operation experiment without a normal terminal reversal at each end. Study how train spacing, local dwell delays and station passenger flow propagate around the loop. Connect the operating model to evidence from underground construction movement, vertical circulation and equipment backup, avoiding the assumption that removing a terminus removes every capacity constraint.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-metro","subcategoryTitle":"都會捷運與貨運","subcategoryTitleEn":"Urban metros and freight","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-metro","learningTags":["rail","rail-metro","station"],"architectureFamily":"rail-system","architectureNodes":[["路線與土建","Alignment and civil works"],["車輛與接觸","Vehicle and contact"],["牽引供電","Traction supply"],["行車控制","Movement control"],["車站與旅客","Stations and passengers"],["監測與維護","Monitoring and maintenance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,1],[3,4],[4,5],[5,0],[5,3]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-system","labels":["路線與土建","車輛與接觸","牽引供電","行車控制","車站與旅客"],"labelsEn":["Alignment and civil works","Vehicle and contact","Traction supply","Movement control","Stations and passengers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合原創算例：單元 1 得 fleet=32 trains；單元 2 得 capacity=17307.69 persons/hour；單元 3 得 dwell=25.02083 s。上述三個結果使用各單元明示的不同邊界，不能任意相加或視為實際工程實測值。以第一單元 cycle 的擾動測試，結果改為 35 trains；學徒需先比較單位、敏感度和假設，再決定是否要細化模型。以哥本哈根環狀地鐵為背景，建立沒有一般端點折返的循環營運實驗。課程研究列車間距、局部停站延誤與車站人流如何沿環線傳遞，並連接地下施工變形、垂直交通和設備備援的驗證資料。 最終交付應保留原始輸入、測點時間戳、誤差範圍與無法由簡化式證明的結論。","textEn":"Integrated original exercise: unit 1 gives fleet=32 trains; unit 2 gives capacity=17307.69 persons/hour; unit 3 gives dwell=25.02083 s. These three results use different explicit boundaries and must not be added or presented as measurements of the real railway. Perturbing cycle in the first unit changes its result to 35 trains. Compare units, sensitivity and assumptions before deciding which model needs refinement. Use Copenhagen Cityringen to construct a circular-operation experiment without a normal terminal reversal at each end. Study how train spacing, local dwell delays and station passenger flow propagate around the loop. Connect the operating model to evidence from underground construction movement, vertical circulation and equipment backup, avoiding the assumption that removing a terminus removes every capacity constraint. The final submission should retain original inputs, measurement timestamps, uncertainty ranges and conclusions that the simplified expressions cannot establish.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b326-v16-s1","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求與班距與有效運能","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement & Headway and usable capacity","description":"本階段聚焦「單圈週期與車隊需求」與「班距與有效運能」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Loop cycle and fleet requirement\" and \"Headway and usable capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b326-v16-01","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「單圈週期與車隊需求」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Loop cycle and fleet requirement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"環狀路線的循環時間是一圈行駛時間加沿途停站時間，不需要假設每圈都在端點換向。以循環時間除以班距並向上取整，可得到維持規則發車的最低運轉車數；如果某站停站延誤，車距不均會沿環線傳播，不能靠沒有終端站就宣稱沒有瓶頸。 循環時間除以班距後必須向上取整，半列車不能提供完整班次。此數量是投入循環的最低值，維修備用、延誤緩衝與不同分支運轉仍需額外配置。 用單圈時間取代雙端折返循環，計算環線所需列車數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「單圈週期與車隊需求」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a circular route, cycle time is one loop of running and station dwell; reversal at a terminal is not required on every circuit. Dividing cycle time by headway and rounding up gives the minimum circulating fleet for regular departures. Delay at one station can propagate uneven spacing around the loop, so absence of a terminus does not imply absence of bottlenecks. Divide cycle time by headway and round upward because a fraction of a train cannot provide a full departure. This is the minimum circulating requirement; maintenance spares, delay buffers and branch-specific operation need additional allocation. Use loop time instead of a two-terminal cycle to calculate trains required on the ring. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Loop cycle and fleet requirement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains.","failure":"常見誤解：「環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「單圈週期與車隊需求」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Loop cycle and fleet requirement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-01-k1","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement","text":"環狀路線的循環時間是一圈行駛時間加沿途停站時間，不需要假設每圈都在端點換向。以循環時間除以班距並向上取整，可得到維持規則發車的最低運轉車數；如果某站停站延誤，車距不均會沿環線傳播，不能靠沒有終端站就宣稱沒有瓶頸。","textEn":"For a circular route, cycle time is one loop of running and station dwell; reversal at a terminal is not required on every circuit. Dividing cycle time by headway and rounding up gives the minimum circulating fleet for regular departures.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單圈週期與車隊需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Loop cycle and fleet requirement\" is correct?","options":["環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數","環狀路線的循環時間是一圈行駛時間加沿途停站時間，不需要假設每圈都在端點換向。","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size.","For a circular route, cycle time is one loop of running and station dwell; reversal at a terminal is not required on every circuit.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"環狀路線的循環時間是一圈行駛時間加沿途停站時間，不需要假設每圈都在端點換向。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a circular route, cycle time is one loop of running and station dwell; reversal at a terminal is not required on every circuit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b326-v16-02","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「單圈週期與車隊需求」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Loop cycle and fleet requirement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。敏感度：cycle 單獨增加百分之十至 6177.6 s，其餘固定，結果為 35 trains。模型邊界：固定周轉與班距、無延誤；不含備用率和維修排程。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Sensitivity: cycle, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 6177.6 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 35 trains. Model boundary: Fixed cycle and headway without delays; reserve ratio and maintenance scheduling are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一列車通過固定參考站兩次的時間差量測單圈週期，逐站記錄停站時間，再重播連續數圈班表，確認每次發車有可用車組。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure loop time between two successive passages of the same train at a fixed reference station.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。敏感度：cycle 單獨增加百分之十至 6177.6 s，其餘固定，結果為 35 trains。模型邊界：固定周轉與班距、無延誤；不含備用率和維修排程。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Sensitivity: cycle, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 6177.6 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 35 trains. Model boundary: Fixed cycle and headway without delays; reserve ratio and maintenance scheduling are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單圈週期與車隊需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Loop cycle and fleet requirement\", which statement holds?","options":["平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達","兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s。"],"optionsEn":["A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.","Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s；計算：fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: cycle=5616 s; headway=180 s; calculation: fleet=ceil(cycle/headway)=32 trains. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b326-v16-03","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「單圈週期與車隊需求」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Loop cycle and fleet requirement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一列車通過固定參考站兩次的時間差量測單圈週期，逐站記錄停站時間，再重播連續數圈班表，確認每次發車有可用車組。若延誤持續累積，應分辨新增車輛、調節停站或進出車場安排的不同效果。 核對單圈行駛、沿途停站與班距使用相同時間單位，以逐列事件表確認每圈都有可用列車。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure loop time between two successive passages of the same train at a fixed reference station. Record dwell at each stop, then replay several circuits to confirm a train is available at every departure. If delay accumulates, distinguish the effects of extra trains, dwell regulation and depot entry or exit. Verify common time units for loop running, station dwell and headway, using a train-by-train event table to confirm availability on every circuit. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：增加一個轉乘站的停站時間並重算單圈週期與向上取整車數，再以逐列時刻表檢查車距不均是否沿環線擴大。另列維修備車，不能把最低運轉車數當成全車隊採購量。 再以本單元 cycle 的對照值重算 fleet，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase dwell at one interchange and recalculate loop time and the upward-rounded train requirement. Replay individual trains to check whether uneven spacing grows around the circle. List maintenance spares separately, rather than treating the minimum circulating count as total fleet procurement. Also recalculate fleet for the alternative cycle value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一列車通過固定參考站兩次的時間差量測單圈週期，逐站記錄停站時間，再重播連續數圈班表，確認每次發車有可用車組。若延誤持續累積，應分辨新增車輛、調節停站或進出車場安排的不同效果。 核對單圈行駛、沿途停站與班距使用相同時間單位，以逐列事件表確認每圈都有可用列車。","textEn":"Measure loop time between two successive passages of the same train at a fixed reference station. Record dwell at each stop, then replay several circuits to confirm a train is available at every departure. If delay accumulates, distinguish the effects of extra trains, dwell regulation and depot entry or exit. Verify common time units for loop running, station dwell and headway, using a train-by-train event table to confirm availability on every circuit.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"增加一個轉乘站的停站時間並重算單圈週期與向上取整車數，再以逐列時刻表檢查車距不均是否沿環線擴大。另列維修備車，不能把最低運轉車數當成全車隊採購量。 再以本單元 cycle 的對照值重算 fleet，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase dwell at one interchange and recalculate loop time and the upward-rounded train requirement. Replay individual trains to check whether uneven spacing grows around the circle. List maintenance spares separately, rather than treating the minimum circulating count as total fleet procurement. Also recalculate fleet for the alternative cycle value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單圈週期與車隊需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Loop cycle and fleet requirement\"?","options":["以同一列車通過固定參考站兩次的時間差量測單圈週期，逐站記錄停站時間，再重播連續數圈班表，確認每次發車有可用車組。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Measure loop time between two successive passages of the same train at a fixed reference station.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一列車通過固定參考站兩次的時間差量測單圈週期，逐站記錄停站時間，再重播連續數圈班表，確認每次發車有可用車組。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure loop time between two successive passages of the same train at a fixed reference station. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b326-v16-04","title":"單圈週期與車隊需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Loop cycle and fleet requirement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「單圈週期與車隊需求」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Loop cycle and fleet requirement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 循環時間稍增可能跨過整數門檻，不能只比較百分比。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A small cycle-time increase can cross an integer fleet threshold; percentages alone are insufficient. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用單圈時間取代雙端折返循環，計算環線所需列車數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Use loop time instead of a two-terminal cycle to calculate trains required on the ring.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 循環時間稍增可能跨過整數門檻，不能只比較百分比。","textEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. A small cycle-time increase can cross an integer fleet threshold; percentages alone are insufficient.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單圈週期與車隊需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Loop cycle and fleet requirement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"列車數足夠仍可能因機廠出入路徑受限而無法準時上線；忽略維修週期則會讓紙上車隊數不可持續。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Sufficient fleet count may still fail when depot access restricts insertion; ignoring maintenance cycles makes the paper fleet unsustainable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b326-v16-05","title":"班距與有效運能：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「班距與有效運能」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Headway and usable capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。車門交換、轉乘尖峰與不均勻到站會讓理論運能無法實現，容量計算應同時報告負載分布。 此式計算的是通過指定斷面的名目服務率，不能表示月台能容納多少人。需求在空間或時間上集中時，某站可以過載，即使整條線的平均載客率仍低。 把環線某站延誤後的實際班距逐班記錄，檢查運能。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「班距與有效運能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. A shorter average headway does not ensure every station can absorb the passenger flow. Door exchange, transfer surges and irregular arrivals can prevent the theoretical rate from being realised, so occupancy distribution must accompany the capacity estimate. This expression estimates a nominal service rate across a specified section, not how many people a platform can hold. Concentrated demand can overload one station even when average occupancy across the complete line remains relatively low. Record successive headways after delay at one loop station and inspect delivered capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Headway and usable capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「班距與有效運能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Headway and usable capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-05-k1","title":"班距與有效運能","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity","text":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。車門交換、轉乘尖峰與不均勻到站會讓理論運能無法實現，容量計算應同時報告負載分布。","textEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. A shorter average headway does not ensure every station can absorb the passenger flow.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「班距與有效運能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Headway and usable capacity\" is correct?","options":["只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半","每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異","每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。"],"optionsEn":["Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.","Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.","Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每小時運能由列車可用容量與通過頻率共同決定，平均班距縮短不代表每個車站都能吸收人流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hourly capacity combines usable train capacity with passage frequency. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b326-v16-06","title":"班距與有效運能：定量估算","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「班距與有效運能」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Headway and usable capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour。敏感度：headway 單獨增加百分之十至 205.92 s/train，其餘固定，結果為 15734.27 persons/hour。模型邊界：固定班距且每列都能使用指定容量；不包含站台壅塞及服務波動。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour. Sensitivity: headway, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 205.92 s/train, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15734.27 persons/hour. Model boundary: Fixed headway with the stated usable capacity on every train; platform congestion and service variability are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour。敏感度：headway 單獨增加百分之十至 205.92 s/train，其餘固定，結果為 15734.27 persons/hour。模型邊界：固定班距且每列都能使用指定容量；不包含站台壅塞及服務波動。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour. Sensitivity: headway, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 205.92 s/train, with all other inputs fixed, gives 15734.27 persons/hour. Model boundary: Fixed headway with the stated usable capacity on every train; platform congestion and service variability are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「班距與有效運能」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Headway and usable capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train；計算：capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: people=900 persons/train; headway=187.2 s/train; calculation: capacity=3600*people/headway=17307.69 persons/hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b326-v16-07","title":"班距與有效運能：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「班距與有效運能」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Headway and usable capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 逐列核對上車、下車與留下人數的守恆，並以同一計數時間窗比較需求和服務量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Carry passengers unable to board into the queue instead of treating rated capacity as delivered service. Check conservation of boarding, alighting and remaining passengers for every train, using identical counting windows for demand and delivered service. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用一組規則班距與一組相同平均值的不規則班距，追蹤每班留下的人數，解釋理論容量與可用容量的差距。 再以本單元 headway 的對照值重算 capacity，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare regular and irregular headways with the same mean, track passengers left behind after each departure, and explain the gap between theoretical and usable capacity. Also recalculate capacity for the alternative headway value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 逐列核對上車、下車與留下人數的守恆，並以同一計數時間窗比較需求和服務量。","textEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Carry passengers unable to board into the queue instead of treating rated capacity as delivered service. Check conservation of boarding, alighting and remaining passengers for every train, using identical counting windows for demand and delivered service.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用一組規則班距與一組相同平均值的不規則班距，追蹤每班留下的人數，解釋理論容量與可用容量的差距。 再以本單元 headway 的對照值重算 capacity，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare regular and irregular headways with the same mean, track passengers left behind after each departure, and explain the gap between theoretical and usable capacity. Also recalculate capacity for the alternative headway value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「班距與有效運能」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Headway and usable capacity\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。","注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads.","Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以連續列車的實際到站時間與逐車廂乘載量重算，將未登車人數保留在隊列，不以列車額定容量代替實際服務量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Recalculate from consecutive arrival times and individual car loads. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b326-v16-08","title":"班距與有效運能：失效診斷","titleEn":"Headway and usable capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「班距與有效運能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Headway and usable capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 應查驗未登車隊列，避免把滿載通過當成需求已服務。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Inspect passengers left behind instead of interpreting a full passing train as demand served. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把環線某站延誤後的實際班距逐班記錄，檢查運能。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Record successive headways after delay at one loop station and inspect delivered capacity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 應查驗未登車隊列，避免把滿載通過當成需求已服務。","textEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Inspect passengers left behind instead of interpreting a full passing train as demand served.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「班距與有效運能」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Headway and usable capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異","某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.","A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail."],"answer":2,"explanation":"某一列延誤會使後車追近而前方隊列累積；只看小時平均會漏掉最擁擠列車與長等待尾端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A delayed train lets following trains bunch while the upstream queue grows; an hourly mean hides both the fullest train and the long-wait tail. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b326-v16-s2","title":"車門交換與停站時間與通訊延遲與位置陳舊量","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time & Communication delay and stale position","description":"本階段聚焦「車門交換與停站時間」與「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Door exchange and dwell time\" and \"Communication delay and stale position\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b326-v16-09","title":"車門交換與停站時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「車門交換與停站時間」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Door exchange and dwell time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"停站時間由車門開關、旅客交換與確認安全三部分組成。把旅客平均分到所有車門只是基準，樓梯位置會使某幾扇門超載；最慢的門組可能控制全列發車，因此不能只用平均流率。 均分模型是檢查單位和量級的起點；真實發車須等最後必要門組完成。上車和下車方向互相干擾時，應用分階段或逐門事件模型重新識別流率。 比較環線各站不均勻交換需求對最大停站時間的控制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「車門交換與停站時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dwell time comprises door movement, passenger exchange and confirmation before departure. Equal distribution across doors is only a baseline: stair placement can overload selected doors. The slowest door group may govern departure of the entire train, so average flow alone is insufficient. Uniform allocation is a starting point for units and scale, while actual departure waits for the last required door group. If boarding and alighting interfere, use phased or door-by-door event models to identify the relevant exchange rates. Compare how uneven station exchange demand controls the longest dwell around the loop. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Door exchange and dwell time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s；計算：dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s; calculation: dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「車門交換與停站時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Door exchange and dwell time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-09-k1","title":"車門交換與停站時間","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time","text":"停站時間由車門開關、旅客交換與確認安全三部分組成。把旅客平均分到所有車門只是基準，樓梯位置會使某幾扇門超載；最慢的門組可能控制全列發車，因此不能只用平均流率。","textEn":"Dwell time comprises door movement, passenger exchange and confirmation before departure. Equal distribution across doors is only a baseline: stair placement can overload selected doors.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「車門交換與停站時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Door exchange and dwell time\" is correct?","options":["停站時間由車門開關、旅客交換與確認安全三部分組成。","每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Dwell time comprises door movement, passenger exchange and confirmation before departure.","Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"停站時間由車門開關、旅客交換與確認安全三部分組成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dwell time comprises door movement, passenger exchange and confirmation before departure. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b326-v16-10","title":"車門交換與停站時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「車門交換與停站時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Door exchange and dwell time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s；計算：dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s。敏感度：exchange 將整數計數增加到 275至 275 persons，其餘固定，結果為 26.32292 s。模型邊界：均勻分配旅客與固定單門流率；不含對向人流衝突。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s; calculation: dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s. Sensitivity: exchange, increase the integer count to 275, to 275 persons, with all other inputs fixed, gives 26.32292 s. Model boundary: Uniform passenger distribution and fixed per-door flow; opposing-flow conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐門標註下車、上車與關門事件，檢查樓梯附近門組是否偏慢，再以各門最大完成時間對照整列停站時間。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Annotate alighting, boarding and closure at each door, check slow groups near stairs, and compare the latest completion time with whole-train dwell.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s；計算：dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s。敏感度：exchange 將整數計數增加到 275至 275 persons，其餘固定，結果為 26.32292 s。模型邊界：均勻分配旅客與固定單門流率；不含對向人流衝突。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s; calculation: dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s. Sensitivity: exchange, increase the integer count to 275, to 275 persons, with all other inputs fixed, gives 26.32292 s. Model boundary: Uniform passenger distribution and fixed per-door flow; opposing-flow conflicts are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「車門交換與停站時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Door exchange and dwell time\", which statement holds?","options":["兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","Original hypothetical exercise.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s；計算：dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: exchange=250 persons; doors=24 doors; rate=0.8 persons/(door*s); fixed=12 s; calculation: dwell=exchange/(doors*rate)+fixed=25.02083 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b326-v16-11","title":"車門交換與停站時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「車門交換與停站時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Door exchange and dwell time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐門標註下車、上車與關門事件，檢查樓梯附近門組是否偏慢，再以各門最大完成時間對照整列停站時間。 以影片事件時間和門控紀錄交叉對時，分別統計交換完成與發車確認的尾端分布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Annotate alighting, boarding and closure at each door, check slow groups near stairs, and compare the latest completion time with whole-train dwell. Synchronise video event times with door-controller logs and separately report the tails of exchange completion and departure confirmation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將一半上車需求集中在四分之一車門，重算最慢門組；提出導引與月台配置改進並區分其對固定時間和交換時間的作用。 再以本單元 exchange 的對照值重算 dwell，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Concentrate half the demand at one quarter of the doors, recalculate the slowest group, and distinguish guidance changes affecting fixed time from those affecting exchange time. Also recalculate dwell for the alternative exchange value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：行李卡門或乘客集中會讓均勻模型低估尾端；延長關門提示可能改善秩序，也可能提高固定停站時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Luggage obstruction and clustered passengers make the uniform model underestimate the tail; a longer closing warning may improve order while increasing the fixed dwell component. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐門標註下車、上車與關門事件，檢查樓梯附近門組是否偏慢，再以各門最大完成時間對照整列停站時間。 以影片事件時間和門控紀錄交叉對時，分別統計交換完成與發車確認的尾端分布。","textEn":"Annotate alighting, boarding and closure at each door, check slow groups near stairs, and compare the latest completion time with whole-train dwell. Synchronise video event times with door-controller logs and separately report the tails of exchange completion and departure confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將一半上車需求集中在四分之一車門，重算最慢門組；提出導引與月台配置改進並區分其對固定時間和交換時間的作用。 再以本單元 exchange 的對照值重算 dwell，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Concentrate half the demand at one quarter of the doors, recalculate the slowest group, and distinguish guidance changes affecting fixed time from those affecting exchange time. Also recalculate dwell for the alternative exchange value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「車門交換與停站時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Door exchange and dwell time\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低","逐門標註下車、上車與關門事件，檢查樓梯附近門組是否偏慢，再以各門最大完成時間對照整列停站時間。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability.","Annotate alighting, boarding and closure at each door, check slow groups near stairs, and compare the latest completion time with whole-train dwell."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐門標註下車、上車與關門事件，檢查樓梯附近門組是否偏慢，再以各門最大完成時間對照整列停站時間。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Annotate alighting, boarding and closure at each door, check slow groups near stairs, and compare the latest completion time with whole-train dwell. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b326-v16-12","title":"車門交換與停站時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Door exchange and dwell time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「車門交換與停站時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Door exchange and dwell time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"行李卡門或乘客集中會讓均勻模型低估尾端；延長關門提示可能改善秩序，也可能提高固定停站時間。 先核對門口人數，避免把旅客集中誤診為門機速度下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Luggage obstruction and clustered passengers make the uniform model underestimate the tail; a longer closing warning may improve order while increasing the fixed dwell component. Check doorway demand before misdiagnosing passenger concentration as slower door machinery. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較環線各站不均勻交換需求對最大停站時間的控制。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare how uneven station exchange demand controls the longest dwell around the loop.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"行李卡門或乘客集中會讓均勻模型低估尾端；延長關門提示可能改善秩序，也可能提高固定停站時間。 先核對門口人數，避免把旅客集中誤診為門機速度下降。","textEn":"Luggage obstruction and clustered passengers make the uniform model underestimate the tail; a longer closing warning may improve order while increasing the fixed dwell component. Check doorway demand before misdiagnosing passenger concentration as slower door machinery.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「車門交換與停站時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Door exchange and dwell time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["行李卡門或乘客集中會讓均勻模型低估尾端；延長關門提示可能改善秩序，也可能提高固定停站時間。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Luggage obstruction and clustered passengers make the uniform model underestimate the tail.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"行李卡門或乘客集中會讓均勻模型低估尾端；延長關門提示可能改善秩序，也可能提高固定停站時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Luggage obstruction and clustered passengers make the uniform model underestimate the tail; a longer closing warning may improve order while increasing the fixed dwell component. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b326-v16-13","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Communication delay and stale position” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。封包延遲、遺失與時鐘偏差應分開，平均延遲不能代表最壞情況，也不能直接替代列車保護的安全論證。 傳輸時間不是訊息年齡的全部，排隊、重送及接收端處理也可能占主要比例。安全邏輯應明確定義逾時後的狀態；成功收到舊封包不能當成最新授權。 檢查循環運轉中授權資料到期如何影響後續列車。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. Speed times delay gives the simplest stale-position bound. Packet delay, loss and clock bias must be separated; mean latency neither represents a worst case nor replaces a safety argument for train protection. Transmission time is not the entire message age; queueing, retransmission and receiver processing may dominate. Safety logic needs an explicit state after timeout. Successful receipt of an old packet is not equivalent to a fresh movement authority. Inspect how authority-data expiry affects following trains during circular operation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Communication delay and stale position” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Communication delay and stale position”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-13-k1","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position","text":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。封包延遲、遺失與時鐘偏差應分開，平均延遲不能代表最壞情況，也不能直接替代列車保護的安全論證。","textEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. Speed times delay gives the simplest stale-position bound.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Communication delay and stale position\" is correct?","options":["平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達","移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差"],"optionsEn":["A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.","A moving train advances while a message is in transit.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"移動列車在訊息傳遞期間繼續前進，最簡單的陳舊位置上界是速度乘延遲。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A moving train advances while a message is in transit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b326-v16-14","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：定量估算","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Communication delay and stale position” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m。敏感度：latency 單獨增加百分之十至 0.3432 s，其餘固定，結果為 8.58 m。模型邊界：固定速度且單次訊息延遲；未含加速度、連續遺失及協定重試。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m. Sensitivity: latency, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.3432 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.58 m. Model boundary: Constant speed and one delayed message; acceleration, consecutive losses and protocol retries are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m。敏感度：latency 單獨增加百分之十至 0.3432 s，其餘固定，結果為 8.58 m。模型邊界：固定速度且單次訊息延遲；未含加速度、連續遺失及協定重試。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m. Sensitivity: latency, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.3432 s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 8.58 m. Model boundary: Constant speed and one delayed message; acceleration, consecutive losses and protocol retries are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Communication delay and stale position\", which statement holds?","options":["風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降","注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s。"],"optionsEn":["A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel.","Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s；計算：stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: v=25 m/s; latency=0.312 s; calculation: stale_distance=v*latency=7.8 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b326-v16-15","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Communication delay and stale position” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 以發送與接收端同步時鐘核對端到端延遲，記錄重送次數、封包遺失及最長連續中斷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Use synchronised sender and receiver clocks to check end-to-end delay, recording retries, packet loss and the longest continuous interruption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把速度與延遲各提高一成，比較位置陳舊量；設計含連續遺失的重播案例，列出接收端需要保留的時間與序號資訊。 再以本單元 latency 的對照值重算 stale_distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Increase speed and delay separately, compare stale distance, and design a replay with consecutive losses listing the timestamps and sequence information required at the receiver. Also recalculate stale_distance for the alternative latency value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 以發送與接收端同步時鐘核對端到端延遲，記錄重送次數、封包遺失及最長連續中斷。","textEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Use synchronised sender and receiver clocks to check end-to-end delay, recording retries, packet loss and the longest continuous interruption.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把速度與延遲各提高一成，比較位置陳舊量；設計含連續遺失的重播案例，列出接收端需要保留的時間與序號資訊。 再以本單元 latency 的對照值重算 stale_distance，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Increase speed and delay separately, compare stale distance, and design a replay with consecutive losses listing the timestamps and sequence information required at the receiver. Also recalculate stale_distance for the alternative latency value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Communication delay and stale position\"?","options":["以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數"],"optionsEn":["Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以送出和接收兩端的同步時間戳量延遲分布，注入延遲及封包遺失，確認過期訊息被辨識而非繼續當成即時位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure latency distribution using synchronised transmit and receive timestamps, inject delay and packet loss, and confirm stale messages are identified rather than treated as current position. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b326-v16-16","title":"通訊延遲與位置陳舊量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Communication delay and stale position: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Communication delay and stale position” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 先檢查序號與時間戳，避免把重播封包誤認為狀態恢復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Check sequence numbers and timestamps before interpreting a replayed packet as state recovery. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查循環運轉中授權資料到期如何影響後續列車。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Inspect how authority-data expiry affects following trains during circular operation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 先檢查序號與時間戳，避免把重播封包誤認為狀態恢復。","textEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Check sequence numbers and timestamps before interpreting a replayed packet as state recovery.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通訊延遲與位置陳舊量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Communication delay and stale position\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時鐘漂移可能讓過期訊息被誤判為新資料；只測低負載網路會漏掉交接區、干擾和突發流量造成的延遲尾端。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Clock drift can make stale data appear fresh; low-load tests miss latency tails caused by handover, interference and burst traffic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b326-v16-s3","title":"里程融合與不確定度與垂直動線有效輸送率","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty & Vertical circulation throughput","description":"本階段聚焦「里程融合與不確定度」與「垂直動線有效輸送率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" and \"Vertical circulation throughput\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b326-v16-17","title":"里程融合與不確定度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「里程融合與不確定度」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Position fusion and uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。輪徑誤差和共同地圖偏差可能讓多個通道一起偏移，不能靠增加感測器數量消除。 兩個獨立無偏估計的資訊量可以相加，較小變異數應獲較大權重。共同偏差不會被這種融合消除，相關性也會破壞公式；較小標準差只能表示宣告模型下的精密度。 在重複繞圈情境中檢查定位偏差是否獲參考點校正。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「里程融合與不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. Wheel-diameter error and shared map bias can shift multiple channels together, so merely adding sensors does not remove systematic error. Information from two independent unbiased estimates can be combined, assigning greater weight to smaller variance. Shared bias is not removed by this fusion, and correlation invalidates the expression. Smaller standard deviation represents precision only under the declared statistical model. Check whether localisation bias is corrected at reference points during repeated circuits. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Position fusion and uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「里程融合與不確定度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Position fusion and uncertainty”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-17-k1","title":"里程融合與不確定度","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty","text":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。輪徑誤差和共同地圖偏差可能讓多個通道一起偏移，不能靠增加感測器數量消除。","textEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. Wheel-diameter error and shared map bias can shift multiple channels together, so merely adding sensors does not remove systematic error.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「里程融合與不確定度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" is correct?","options":["兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。"],"optionsEn":["Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected."],"answer":2,"explanation":"獨立位置感測器可用變異數倒數加權，但只有誤差不相關且偏差已校正時，融合後不確定度才按公式下降。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Independent position measurements can be weighted by inverse variance, but uncertainty decreases as predicted only when errors are uncorrelated and biases have been corrected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b326-v16-18","title":"里程融合與不確定度：定量估算","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「里程融合與不確定度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Position fusion and uncertainty” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m。敏感度：s1 單獨增加百分之十至 4.576 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.832609 m。模型邊界：零均值獨立高斯誤差；不含共同偏差與完整性風險。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m. Sensitivity: s1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 4.576 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.832609 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean Gaussian errors; common bias and integrity risk are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m。敏感度：s1 單獨增加百分之十至 4.576 m，其餘固定，結果為 1.832609 m。模型邊界：零均值獨立高斯誤差；不含共同偏差與完整性風險。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m. Sensitivity: s1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 4.576 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 1.832609 m. Model boundary: Independent zero-mean Gaussian errors; common bias and integrity risk are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「里程融合與不確定度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Position fusion and uncertainty\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m；計算：sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: s1=4.16 m; s2=2 m; calculation: sigma=(1/(1/s1**2+1/s2**2))**0.5=1.802505 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b326-v16-19","title":"里程融合與不確定度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「里程融合與不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Position fusion and uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 以外部參考位置核對兩感測器殘差，檢查平均偏差及相關係數，再比較融合後覆蓋範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Check both sensor residuals against an external position reference, examine mean bias and correlation, and compare coverage after fusion. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立獨立誤差與共同偏差兩組資料，對比融合結果，指出哪一種誤差需要外部控制點才能發現。 再以本單元 s1 的對照值重算 sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct independent-error and common-bias datasets, compare their fused results, and identify the error requiring an external control point for detection. Also recalculate sigma for the alternative s1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 以外部參考位置核對兩感測器殘差，檢查平均偏差及相關係數，再比較融合後覆蓋範圍。","textEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Check both sensor residuals against an external position reference, examine mean bias and correlation, and compare coverage after fusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立獨立誤差與共同偏差兩組資料，對比融合結果，指出哪一種誤差需要外部控制點才能發現。 再以本單元 s1 的對照值重算 sigma，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct independent-error and common-bias datasets, compare their fused results, and identify the error requiring an external control point for detection. Also recalculate sigma for the alternative s1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「里程融合與不確定度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Position fusion and uncertainty\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以獨立已知控制點比較融合前後殘差，逐段檢查偏差及相關性，並故意遮蔽一個感測器觀察降級行為。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare pre-fusion and post-fusion residuals at independently surveyed points, check bias and correlation by segment, and mask one sensor to inspect degraded operation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b326-v16-20","title":"里程融合與不確定度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Position fusion and uncertainty: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「里程融合與不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Position fusion and uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 若兩感測器共用錯誤基準，融合後仍會保持共同偏差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. If both sensors share a wrong reference, the fused result retains the common bias. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：在重複繞圈情境中檢查定位偏差是否獲參考點校正。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check whether localisation bias is corrected at reference points during repeated circuits.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 若兩感測器共用錯誤基準，融合後仍會保持共同偏差。","textEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. If both sensors share a wrong reference, the fused result retains the common bias.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「里程融合與不確定度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Position fusion and uncertainty\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共用錯誤地圖會讓兩個感測器看似一致卻都錯；錯把相關訊號當獨立會使報告的置信區間過窄。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shared wrong map can make two sensors agree while both are wrong; treating correlated signals as independent produces an overconfident interval. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b326-v16-21","title":"垂直動線有效輸送率：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vertical circulation throughput: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「垂直動線有效輸送率」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vertical circulation throughput” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"電扶梯的理論輸送率可由速度、梯級間距及每級人數估算，實際值還受入口遲疑、行李和站立習慣限制。多台設備不一定能線性相加，因為共用入口或出口可能先形成瓶頸。 階梯間距與速度決定理論階梯通過率，每階占用率則把機械運動轉成載客量。旅客猶豫、行李及出口壅塞會降低實際通過率，不能以理論值直接證明疏散能力。 把深層車站垂直移動與出口步行時間分開量測。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂直動線有效輸送率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Escalator theoretical throughput follows speed, step pitch and occupants per step. Hesitation, luggage and standing habits limit actual use. Several escalators do not necessarily add linearly when a shared entrance or exit becomes the earlier bottleneck. Step pitch and speed determine theoretical step passage, while occupancy per step converts mechanical motion into passenger flow. Hesitation, luggage and blocked exits reduce delivery, so the theoretical rate cannot directly demonstrate evacuation capacity. Measure deep-station vertical travel separately from walking to the exit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vertical circulation throughput” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step；計算：throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step; calculation: throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「垂直動線有效輸送率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vertical circulation throughput”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-21-k1","title":"垂直動線有效輸送率","titleEn":"Vertical circulation throughput","text":"電扶梯的理論輸送率可由速度、梯級間距及每級人數估算，實際值還受入口遲疑、行李和站立習慣限制。多台設備不一定能線性相加，因為共用入口或出口可能先形成瓶頸。","textEn":"Escalator theoretical throughput follows speed, step pitch and occupants per step. Hesitation, luggage and standing habits limit actual use.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直動線有效輸送率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vertical circulation throughput\" is correct?","options":["電扶梯的理論輸送率可由速度、梯級間距及每級人數估算，實際值還受入口遲疑、行李和站立習慣限制。","兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降"],"optionsEn":["Escalator theoretical throughput follows speed, step pitch and occupants per step.","Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"電扶梯的理論輸送率可由速度、梯級間距及每級人數估算，實際值還受入口遲疑、行李和站立習慣限制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Escalator theoretical throughput follows speed, step pitch and occupants per step. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b326-v16-22","title":"垂直動線有效輸送率：定量估算","titleEn":"Vertical circulation throughput: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂直動線有效輸送率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vertical circulation throughput” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step；計算：throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour。敏感度：speed 單獨增加百分之十至 0.572 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 6177.6 persons/hour。模型邊界：穩定速度和平均梯級占用；不含出入口匯流與無障礙替代路徑。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step; calculation: throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour. Sensitivity: speed, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.572 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 6177.6 persons/hour. Model boundary: Steady speed and mean step occupancy; entrance merging and accessible alternative routes are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐時段計數入口和出口，記錄空梯級比例與行李比例，並在共用平台量隊列長度，避免把額定值當現場值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Count entrance and exit flow by interval, record empty-step and luggage fractions, and measure the shared-landing queue rather than substituting rated throughput.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step；計算：throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour。敏感度：speed 單獨增加百分之十至 0.572 m/s，其餘固定，結果為 6177.6 persons/hour。模型邊界：穩定速度和平均梯級占用；不含出入口匯流與無障礙替代路徑。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step; calculation: throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour. Sensitivity: speed, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.572 m/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 6177.6 persons/hour. Model boundary: Steady speed and mean step occupancy; entrance merging and accessible alternative routes are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂直動線有效輸送率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vertical circulation throughput\", which statement holds?","options":["注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step。","環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數"],"optionsEn":["Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step；計算：throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: speed=0.52 m/s; pitch=0.4 m/step; occupants=1.2 persons/step; calculation: throughput=3600*speed/pitch*occupants=5616 persons/hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b326-v16-23","title":"垂直動線有效輸送率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vertical circulation throughput: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂直動線有效輸送率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vertical circulation throughput” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐時段計數入口和出口，記錄空梯級比例與行李比例，並在共用平台量隊列長度，避免把額定值當現場值。 核對階梯間距與帶速，以入口及出口計數比較乘客流量，另記停頓和空階比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Count entrance and exit flow by interval, record empty-step and luggage fractions, and measure the shared-landing queue rather than substituting rated throughput. Verify step pitch and belt speed, compare entry and exit passenger counts, and separately record stoppages and empty-step proportions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較一台停機與出口縮窄兩種情境，畫出瓶頸位置，提出電梯與樓梯的替代動線並記錄不同旅客所需時間。 再以本單元 speed 的對照值重算 throughput，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare one failed escalator with a narrowed exit, map the bottleneck, and propose lift and stair alternatives while recording journey times for different passenger needs. Also recalculate throughput for the alternative speed value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：出口暫停會造成回堵並影響整段動線；一台設備停機時，另一台的入口可能無法吸收全部轉移人流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A pause at the exit causes spillback through the circulation path; when one escalator is unavailable, the other entrance may not accept all diverted passengers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐時段計數入口和出口，記錄空梯級比例與行李比例，並在共用平台量隊列長度，避免把額定值當現場值。 核對階梯間距與帶速，以入口及出口計數比較乘客流量，另記停頓和空階比例。","textEn":"Count entrance and exit flow by interval, record empty-step and luggage fractions, and measure the shared-landing queue rather than substituting rated throughput. Verify step pitch and belt speed, compare entry and exit passenger counts, and separately record stoppages and empty-step proportions.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較一台停機與出口縮窄兩種情境，畫出瓶頸位置，提出電梯與樓梯的替代動線並記錄不同旅客所需時間。 再以本單元 speed 的對照值重算 throughput，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare one failed escalator with a narrowed exit, map the bottleneck, and propose lift and stair alternatives while recording journey times for different passenger needs. Also recalculate throughput for the alternative speed value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂直動線有效輸送率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vertical circulation throughput\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異","逐時段計數入口和出口，記錄空梯級比例與行李比例，並在共用平台量隊列長度，避免把額定值當現場值。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.","Count entrance and exit flow by interval, record empty-step and luggage fractions, and measure the shared-landing queue rather than substituting rated throughput."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐時段計數入口和出口，記錄空梯級比例與行李比例，並在共用平台量隊列長度，避免把額定值當現場值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Count entrance and exit flow by interval, record empty-step and luggage fractions, and measure the shared-landing queue rather than substituting rated throughput. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b326-v16-24","title":"垂直動線有效輸送率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vertical circulation throughput: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂直動線有效輸送率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vertical circulation throughput” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"出口暫停會造成回堵並影響整段動線；一台設備停機時，另一台的入口可能無法吸收全部轉移人流。 出口堵塞時提高帶速可能加劇累積，需先檢查出口容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A pause at the exit causes spillback through the circulation path; when one escalator is unavailable, the other entrance may not accept all diverted passengers. Increasing belt speed can worsen accumulation at a blocked outlet; inspect outlet capacity first. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把深層車站垂直移動與出口步行時間分開量測。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measure deep-station vertical travel separately from walking to the exit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"出口暫停會造成回堵並影響整段動線；一台設備停機時，另一台的入口可能無法吸收全部轉移人流。 出口堵塞時提高帶速可能加劇累積，需先檢查出口容量。","textEn":"A pause at the exit causes spillback through the circulation path; when one escalator is unavailable, the other entrance may not accept all diverted passengers. Increasing belt speed can worsen accumulation at a blocked outlet; inspect outlet capacity first.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂直動線有效輸送率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vertical circulation throughput\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["出口暫停會造成回堵並影響整段動線；一台設備停機時，另一台的入口可能無法吸收全部轉移人流。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降"],"optionsEn":["A pause at the exit causes spillback through the circulation path; when one escalator is unavailable, the other entrance may not accept all diverted passengers.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"出口暫停會造成回堵並影響整段動線；一台設備停機時，另一台的入口可能無法吸收全部轉移人流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A pause at the exit causes spillback through the circulation path; when one escalator is unavailable, the other entrance may not accept all diverted passengers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b326-v16-s4","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間與沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time & Differential settlement and track kink","description":"本階段聚焦「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」與「沉陷差與軌道坡折」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time\" and \"Differential settlement and track kink\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b326-v16-25","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"完全混合空間的濃度在定風量清除下呈指數衰減，體積除以風量給出特徵時間。真實隧道存在分層、死角及列車活塞風，因此這個模型只適合示範稀釋量級，不能直接用作火災避難判定。 完全混合且污染源已停止時，濃度以指數衰減；剩餘比例必須介於零與一。換氣率是流量除以容積，清除時間還依目標濃度而變，不能把一次換氣直接當成全部清除。 比較深層站有效通風容積與換氣率的單位定義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A perfectly mixed volume under constant clean-air flow exhibits exponential concentration decay, with volume divided by flow as the time constant. Real tunnels contain layering, stagnant regions and train-induced piston flow. This model illustrates dilution scale and cannot establish fire evacuation tenability. For perfect mixing after the source stops, concentration decays exponentially and the remaining fraction lies between zero and one. Air-change rate is flow divided by volume, while clearance time also depends on target concentration. One air change does not mean complete removal. Compare effective deep-station ventilation volume with the units used for air-change rate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1；計算：dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1; calculation: dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-25-k1","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time","text":"完全混合空間的濃度在定風量清除下呈指數衰減，體積除以風量給出特徵時間。真實隧道存在分層、死角及列車活塞風，因此這個模型只適合示範稀釋量級，不能直接用作火災避難判定。","textEn":"A perfectly mixed volume under constant clean-air flow exhibits exponential concentration decay, with volume divided by flow as the time constant. Real tunnels contain layering, stagnant regions and train-induced piston flow.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time\" is correct?","options":["風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降","完全混合空間的濃度在定風量清除下呈指數衰減，體積除以風量給出特徵時間。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel.","A perfectly mixed volume under constant clean-air flow exhibits exponential concentration decay, with volume divided by flow as the time constant.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"完全混合空間的濃度在定風量清除下呈指數衰減，體積除以風量給出特徵時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A perfectly mixed volume under constant clean-air flow exhibits exponential concentration decay, with volume divided by flow as the time constant. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b326-v16-26","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1；計算：dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s。敏感度：flow 單獨增加百分之十至 28.6 m^3/s，其餘固定，結果為 241.5299 s。模型邊界：完全混合且污染源已停止；不含煙層、熱浮力與火災成長。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1; calculation: dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s. Sensitivity: flow, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.6 m^3/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 241.5299 s. Model boundary: Perfect mixing after source removal; smoke layers, buoyancy and fire growth are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用非危險示蹤試驗在不同高度與距離採樣，量測實際風量並檢查濃度衰減是否符合單一指數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use a harmless tracer test with samples at several heights and distances, measure actual airflow, and check whether one exponential describes the decay.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1；計算：dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s。敏感度：flow 單獨增加百分之十至 28.6 m^3/s，其餘固定，結果為 241.5299 s。模型邊界：完全混合且污染源已停止；不含煙層、熱浮力與火災成長。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1; calculation: dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s. Sensitivity: flow, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 28.6 m^3/s, with all other inputs fixed, gives 241.5299 s. Model boundary: Perfect mixing after source removal; smoke layers, buoyancy and fire growth are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time\", which statement holds?","options":["只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低","只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability.","Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1；計算：dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: volume=3000 m^3; flow=26 m^3/s; remaining=0.1 1; calculation: dilution_time=-volume/flow*log(remaining)=265.6829 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b326-v16-27","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用非危險示蹤試驗在不同高度與距離採樣，量測實際風量並檢查濃度衰減是否符合單一指數。 以安全示蹤氣體衰減核對時間常數，多點量測濃度並保留門狀態，檢查是否存在未停止源。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use a harmless tracer test with samples at several heights and distances, measure actual airflow, and check whether one exponential describes the decay. Check the time constant with safe tracer decay, measure concentration at multiple points, retain door states, and check for a continuing source. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對兩種風量計算達到同一殘餘比例的時間，加入一個不完全混合死角，說明量測配置如何發現模型失配。 再以本單元 flow 的對照值重算 dilution_time，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate time to one residual fraction at two airflows, add a poorly mixed pocket, and explain how sensor placement can reveal model mismatch. Also recalculate dilution_time for the alternative flow value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：死角可能在平均濃度下降後仍維持高濃度；風機反轉或風門錯位也會改變流路，不能只用風機啟動回饋判斷通風。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Stagnant pockets may remain concentrated after the average falls; reversed fans or misplaced dampers alter flow paths, so a running-status signal alone cannot verify ventilation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用非危險示蹤試驗在不同高度與距離採樣，量測實際風量並檢查濃度衰減是否符合單一指數。 以安全示蹤氣體衰減核對時間常數，多點量測濃度並保留門狀態，檢查是否存在未停止源。","textEn":"Use a harmless tracer test with samples at several heights and distances, measure actual airflow, and check whether one exponential describes the decay. Check the time constant with safe tracer decay, measure concentration at multiple points, retain door states, and check for a continuing source.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對兩種風量計算達到同一殘餘比例的時間，加入一個不完全混合死角，說明量測配置如何發現模型失配。 再以本單元 flow 的對照值重算 dilution_time，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Calculate time to one residual fraction at two airflows, add a poorly mixed pocket, and explain how sensor placement can reveal model mismatch. Also recalculate dilution_time for the alternative flow value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time\"?","options":["用非危險示蹤試驗在不同高度與距離採樣，量測實際風量並檢查濃度衰減是否符合單一指數。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Use a harmless tracer test with samples at several heights and distances, measure actual airflow, and check whether one exponential describes the decay.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用非危險示蹤試驗在不同高度與距離採樣，量測實際風量並檢查濃度衰減是否符合單一指數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use a harmless tracer test with samples at several heights and distances, measure actual airflow, and check whether one exponential describes the decay. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b326-v16-28","title":"隧道換氣與稀釋時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel air exchange and dilution time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"死角可能在平均濃度下降後仍維持高濃度；風機反轉或風門錯位也會改變流路，不能只用風機啟動回饋判斷通風。 風機有轉不代表有效稀釋，需查風道旁通和持續污染源。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Stagnant pockets may remain concentrated after the average falls; reversed fans or misplaced dampers alter flow paths, so a running-status signal alone cannot verify ventilation. A running fan does not prove effective dilution; inspect bypass and continuing contaminant sources. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較深層站有效通風容積與換氣率的單位定義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare effective deep-station ventilation volume with the units used for air-change rate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"死角可能在平均濃度下降後仍維持高濃度；風機反轉或風門錯位也會改變流路，不能只用風機啟動回饋判斷通風。 風機有轉不代表有效稀釋，需查風道旁通和持續污染源。","textEn":"Stagnant pockets may remain concentrated after the average falls; reversed fans or misplaced dampers alter flow paths, so a running-status signal alone cannot verify ventilation. A running fan does not prove effective dilution; inspect bypass and continuing contaminant sources.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「隧道換氣與稀釋時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Tunnel air exchange and dilution time\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","死角可能在平均濃度下降後仍維持高濃度；風機反轉或風門錯位也會改變流路，不能只用風機啟動回饋判斷通風。","兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Stagnant pockets may remain concentrated after the average falls.","Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them."],"answer":1,"explanation":"死角可能在平均濃度下降後仍維持高濃度；風機反轉或風門錯位也會改變流路，不能只用風機啟動回饋判斷通風。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stagnant pockets may remain concentrated after the average falls; reversed fans or misplaced dampers alter flow paths, so a running-status signal alone cannot verify ventilation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b326-v16-29","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential settlement and track kink” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。 相同端點坡度可以對應完全不同的中間形狀，因此坡度不能單獨表示軌道曲率。測點間距必須小於欲辨認的變形尺度，並將高程誤差相對於基長傳遞到坡度結果。 對施工鄰近建築建立多點沉陷剖面與穩定外部基準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉陷差與軌道坡折」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak. A spatial profile is needed to identify curvature and deformation length. Identical endpoint gradient can hide very different intermediate shapes, so gradient alone cannot describe track curvature. Survey spacing must resolve the deformation length scale, and elevation uncertainty must be propagated relative to the baseline into the reported gradient. Build multipoint settlement profiles and a stable external datum for buildings near construction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential settlement and track kink” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential settlement and track kink”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-29-k1","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink","text":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。兩端高差除以基長只給平均坡度，無法描述局部尖峰；需要多點剖面才能辨認曲率與變形長度。","textEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. End-to-end difference divided by baseline gives only an average gradient, not a local peak.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential settlement and track kink\" is correct?","options":["兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷","注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞","均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。"],"optionsEn":["Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.","Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.","Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"均勻沉陷主要改變高程，短距離差異沉陷則改變軌道坡度和車輪動態荷載。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform settlement mainly changes elevation, whereas differential settlement over a short distance alters track slope and dynamic wheel loading. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b326-v16-30","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential settlement and track kink” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.013728 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.6864 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.013728 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.6864 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m。敏感度：drop 單獨增加百分之十至 0.013728 m，其餘固定，結果為 0.6864 mm/m。模型邊界：小變形平均坡度；不計車軌耦合動力或容許軌道幾何。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m. Sensitivity: drop, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.013728 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.6864 mm/m. Model boundary: Small-deformation average gradient; vehicle-track dynamics and permissible geometry limits are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential settlement and track kink\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m。","環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數","每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical exercise.","A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size.","Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m；計算：gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: drop=0.01248 m; baseline=20 m; calculation: gradient=1000*drop/baseline=0.624 mm/m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b326-v16-31","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential settlement and track kink” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 重複觀測同一測點並做閉合檢核，以另一穩定基準核對零點，報告高差與基長各自誤差。","textEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Repeat identical points with closure checks, verify zero against another stable reference, and report separate errors for elevation difference and baseline.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"構造端點相同但中間下陷的剖面，與直線坡度模型比較；提出足以辨識沉陷槽寬度的測點間距與複測頻率。 再以本單元 drop 的對照值重算 gradient，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Construct a profile with equal endpoints and an intermediate trough, compare it with a straight-gradient model, and propose spacing and repeat intervals able to resolve the trough. Also recalculate gradient for the alternative drop value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉陷差與軌道坡折」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential settlement and track kink\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採用同一穩定水準基點反覆量測，保留溫度和施工時間，利用多點高程剖面區分整段平移、坡折與量測基點漂移。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat surveys against one stable datum, retain temperature and construction timing, and use multipoint profiles to separate translation, kinks and datum drift. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b326-v16-32","title":"沉陷差與軌道坡折：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential settlement and track kink: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉陷差與軌道坡折」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential settlement and track kink” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：對施工鄰近建築建立多點沉陷剖面與穩定外部基準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Build multipoint settlement profiles and a stable external datum for buildings near construction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩端高程相同就能證明兩點之間沒有差異沉陷」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal endpoint elevations prove there is no differential settlement between them.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 高差異常需先查基點，不能立刻推定路基局部下沉。","textEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. An unusual level difference requires a datum check before inferring local earthwork settlement.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉陷差與軌道坡折」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential settlement and track kink\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞","基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.","A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基點本身下沉會讓全段看似正常；只量端點又會漏掉中間沉陷槽，兩種情況均可低估輪軌衝擊。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A settling datum can hide movement of the whole section, and endpoint-only measurement misses an intermediate trough; both may understate wheel-rail impact. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b326-v16-s5","title":"注漿量與空隙體積與並聯備援與共同原因","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account & Parallel redundancy and common cause","description":"本階段聚焦「注漿量與空隙體積」與「並聯備援與共同原因」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Grout volume and void account\" and \"Parallel redundancy and common cause\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b326-v16-33","title":"注漿量與空隙體積：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「注漿量與空隙體積」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grout volume and void account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"填充空隙所需漿量先由幾何空隙體積估算，再考慮損失與材料體積變化。注入量大不代表填充完整，因為漿液可能沿裂縫流失；壓力、流量與返漿紀錄必須互相對照。 此算例把空隙視為長乘寬乘均勻厚度的薄層，再乘假定餘量。它不是完整圓環幾何；若用於環隙局部展開，須說明薄層近似，且不能由注入總量推論填充均勻。 以局部展開的薄層空隙估算灌漿量，區分理論體積與實注量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「注漿量與空隙體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Required grout begins with geometric void volume and allowances for loss and volume change. A large injected volume does not prove complete filling because grout can escape through cracks. Pressure, flow and returns must be interpreted together to distinguish filling from loss. This example treats a void as length times width times uniform thickness with an assumed allowance. It is not full annular geometry. A locally unwrapped annulus requires an explicit thin-layer approximation, and total injection does not establish uniform filling. Estimate grout for a locally unwrapped thin void, distinguishing theoretical from injected volume. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grout volume and void account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1；計算：grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1; calculation: grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3.","failure":"常見誤解：「注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「注漿量與空隙體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grout volume and void account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-33-k1","title":"注漿量與空隙體積","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account","text":"填充空隙所需漿量先由幾何空隙體積估算，再考慮損失與材料體積變化。注入量大不代表填充完整，因為漿液可能沿裂縫流失；壓力、流量與返漿紀錄必須互相對照。","textEn":"Required grout begins with geometric void volume and allowances for loss and volume change. A large injected volume does not prove complete filling because grout can escape through cracks.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「注漿量與空隙體積」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Grout volume and void account\" is correct?","options":["填充空隙所需漿量先由幾何空隙體積估算，再考慮損失與材料體積變化。","注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞","只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低"],"optionsEn":["Required grout begins with geometric void volume and allowances for loss and volume change.","Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.","Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"填充空隙所需漿量先由幾何空隙體積估算，再考慮損失與材料體積變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Required grout begins with geometric void volume and allowances for loss and volume change. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b326-v16-34","title":"注漿量與空隙體積：定量估算","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「注漿量與空隙體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grout volume and void account” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1；計算：grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3。敏感度：gap 單獨增加百分之十至 0.04576 m，其餘固定，結果為 2.6312 m^3。模型邊界：均勻幾何間隙與假設損失係數；不指定注漿壓力或現地工法。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1; calculation: grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3. Sensitivity: gap, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.04576 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2.6312 m^3. Model boundary: Uniform geometric gap and assumed loss allowance; no injection pressure or field procedure is specified. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對批次體積、流量計及返漿量，將注入壓力與時間曲線同步，完成後以獨立檢測確認空隙分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile batch volume, flow meter and returns, synchronise injection pressure over time, and verify void distribution afterward using an independent inspection method.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1；計算：grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3。敏感度：gap 單獨增加百分之十至 0.04576 m，其餘固定，結果為 2.6312 m^3。模型邊界：均勻幾何間隙與假設損失係數；不指定注漿壓力或現地工法。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1; calculation: grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3. Sensitivity: gap, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.04576 m, with all other inputs fixed, gives 2.6312 m^3. Model boundary: Uniform geometric gap and assumed loss allowance; no injection pressure or field procedure is specified.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「注漿量與空隙體積」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Grout volume and void account\", which statement holds?","options":["只要平均班距減半所有乘客的等待時間就一定減半","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1。","平均網路延遲很低就足以證明所有控制訊息都及時到達"],"optionsEn":["Halving average headway necessarily halves the waiting time of every passenger.","Original hypothetical exercise.","A low average network delay proves that every control message arrives on time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1；計算：grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: length=20 m; width=2.5 m; gap=0.0416 m; allowance=1.15 1; calculation: grout_volume=length*width*gap*allowance=2.392 m^3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b326-v16-35","title":"注漿量與空隙體積：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「注漿量與空隙體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grout volume and void account” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對批次體積、流量計及返漿量，將注入壓力與時間曲線同步，完成後以獨立檢測確認空隙分布。 校對泵送流量計與漿液批次密度，分開累計注入、回流及廢棄量，核對薄層幾何尺寸。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile batch volume, flow meter and returns, synchronise injection pressure over time, and verify void distribution afterward using an independent inspection method. Calibrate pump flow and batch density, separately total injection, return and waste volumes, and verify the thin-layer dimensions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較正常填充與沿裂縫漏失兩組流量壓力紀錄，做體積收支並提出能辨識兩者的獨立檢測。 再以本單元 gap 的對照值重算 grout_volume，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare flow-pressure records for normal filling and crack leakage, build a volume balance, and propose an independent inspection that distinguishes the two. Also recalculate grout_volume for the alternative gap value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：漏失會讓注入體積增加而空隙仍未填滿，局部封堵又會使壓力快速上升；僅憑達到預算漿量不能驗收。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Loss can increase injected volume while leaving a void unfilled, and local blockage can raise pressure rapidly; reaching the budgeted volume is not acceptance evidence. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對批次體積、流量計及返漿量，將注入壓力與時間曲線同步，完成後以獨立檢測確認空隙分布。 校對泵送流量計與漿液批次密度，分開累計注入、回流及廢棄量，核對薄層幾何尺寸。","textEn":"Reconcile batch volume, flow meter and returns, synchronise injection pressure over time, and verify void distribution afterward using an independent inspection method. Calibrate pump flow and batch density, separately total injection, return and waste volumes, and verify the thin-layer dimensions.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較正常填充與沿裂縫漏失兩組流量壓力紀錄，做體積收支並提出能辨識兩者的獨立檢測。 再以本單元 gap 的對照值重算 grout_volume，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Compare flow-pressure records for normal filling and crack leakage, build a volume balance, and propose an independent inspection that distinguishes the two. Also recalculate grout_volume for the alternative gap value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「注漿量與空隙體積」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Grout volume and void account\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩台電扶梯的實際總輸送率必定等於單台額定值兩倍","核對批次體積、流量計及返漿量，將注入壓力與時間曲線同步，完成後以獨立檢測確認空隙分布。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Two escalators necessarily deliver twice the rated throughput of one escalator.","Reconcile batch volume, flow meter and returns, synchronise injection pressure over time, and verify void distribution afterward using an independent inspection method."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對批次體積、流量計及返漿量，將注入壓力與時間曲線同步，完成後以獨立檢測確認空隙分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile batch volume, flow meter and returns, synchronise injection pressure over time, and verify void distribution afterward using an independent inspection method. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b326-v16-36","title":"注漿量與空隙體積：失效診斷","titleEn":"Grout volume and void account: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「注漿量與空隙體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grout volume and void account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏失會讓注入體積增加而空隙仍未填滿，局部封堵又會使壓力快速上升；僅憑達到預算漿量不能驗收。 達到預算漿量不等於填滿空隙，須查回流和漏失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Loss can increase injected volume while leaving a void unfilled, and local blockage can raise pressure rapidly; reaching the budgeted volume is not acceptance evidence. Reaching the budgeted grout volume does not prove void filling; inspect returns and losses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以局部展開的薄層空隙估算灌漿量，區分理論體積與實注量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Estimate grout for a locally unwrapped thin void, distinguishing theoretical from injected volume.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「注入漿量超過幾何空隙體積就能證明沒有殘留空洞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Injecting more than the geometric void volume proves that no void remains.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏失會讓注入體積增加而空隙仍未填滿，局部封堵又會使壓力快速上升；僅憑達到預算漿量不能驗收。 達到預算漿量不等於填滿空隙，須查回流和漏失。","textEn":"Loss can increase injected volume while leaving a void unfilled, and local blockage can raise pressure rapidly; reaching the budgeted volume is not acceptance evidence. Reaching the budgeted grout volume does not prove void filling; inspect returns and losses.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「注漿量與空隙體積」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Grout volume and void account\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏失會讓注入體積增加而空隙仍未填滿，局部封堵又會使壓力快速上升；僅憑達到預算漿量不能驗收。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低"],"optionsEn":["Loss can increase injected volume while leaving a void unfilled, and local blockage can raise pressure rapidly.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏失會讓注入體積增加而空隙仍未填滿，局部封堵又會使壓力快速上升；僅憑達到預算漿量不能驗收。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Loss can increase injected volume while leaving a void unfilled, and local blockage can raise pressure rapidly; reaching the budgeted volume is not acceptance evidence. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b326-v16-37","title":"並聯備援與共同原因：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel redundancy and common cause: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「並聯備援與共同原因」如何影響哥本哈根地鐵環狀線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel redundancy and common cause” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Copenhagen Cityringen”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩個獨立元件只要有一個成功即可服務時，系統失效機率等於兩者失效機率相乘。但共用電源、軟體或環境會破壞獨立假設，備援數量增加不能自動證明整體風險按平方下降。 獨立失效機率相乘只在共同原因可忽略時成立。共用機房、電源、時鐘或軟體缺陷會使冗餘失去預期效果；應把獨立事件與共同事件分成不同邏輯項。 檢查環線控制備援是否仍受同一供電或機房事件影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯備援與共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When either of two independent components can serve the demand, system failure probability is the product of their failure probabilities. Shared power, software or environment breaks independence. More redundant components therefore do not automatically prove a squared reduction in overall risk. Multiplying failure probabilities requires negligible common causes. Shared rooms, power, clocks or software defects can defeat expected redundancy. Represent independent events and common events as separate logical terms rather than silently combining them. Check whether ring-control redundancy remains exposed to one supply or equipment-room event. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel redundancy and common cause” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1；計算：joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1; calculation: joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「並聯備援與共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel redundancy and common cause”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-37-k1","title":"並聯備援與共同原因","titleEn":"Parallel redundancy and common cause","text":"兩個獨立元件只要有一個成功即可服務時，系統失效機率等於兩者失效機率相乘。但共用電源、軟體或環境會破壞獨立假設，備援數量增加不能自動證明整體風險按平方下降。","textEn":"When either of two independent components can serve the demand, system failure probability is the product of their failure probabilities. Shared power, software or environment breaks independence.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「並聯備援與共同原因」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel redundancy and common cause\" is correct?","options":["只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低","兩個獨立元件只要有一個成功即可服務時，系統失效機率等於兩者失效機率相乘。","環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數"],"optionsEn":["Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability.","When either of two independent components can serve the demand, system failure probability is the product of their failure probabilities.","A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩個獨立元件只要有一個成功即可服務時，系統失效機率等於兩者失效機率相乘。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When either of two independent components can serve the demand, system failure probability is the product of their failure probabilities. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b326-v16-38","title":"並聯備援與共同原因：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel redundancy and common cause: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「並聯備援與共同原因」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel redundancy and common cause” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1；計算：joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1。敏感度：q1 單獨增加百分之十至 0.02288 1，其餘固定，結果為 0.0006864 1。模型邊界：同一時間窗內獨立失效且切換完美；不含共同原因與切換失敗。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1; calculation: joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1. Sensitivity: q1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.02288 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.0006864 1. Model boundary: Independent failures in one time window with perfect switching; common causes and switch failure are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：畫出供電、網路、冷卻和軟體版本的依賴圖，逐一驗證切換功能；以故障注入確認另一通道可承接完整需求。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Map dependencies in power, networking, cooling and software versions, verify switching, and use fault injection to confirm the surviving channel can carry the full demand.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1；計算：joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1。敏感度：q1 單獨增加百分之十至 0.02288 1，其餘固定，結果為 0.0006864 1。模型邊界：同一時間窗內獨立失效且切換完美；不含共同原因與切換失敗。","textEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1; calculation: joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1. Sensitivity: q1, increase this input alone by ten percent, to 0.02288 1, with all other inputs fixed, gives 0.0006864 1. Model boundary: Independent failures in one time window with perfect switching; common causes and switch failure are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「並聯備援與共同原因」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel redundancy and common cause\", which statement holds?","options":["每扇門的平均流率相同就能忽略乘客分布差異","兩個定位來源彼此一致就能保證定位沒有共同偏差","原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1；計算：joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1。"],"optionsEn":["Equal average door flow rates make passenger distribution irrelevant to dwell time.","Agreement between two position sources guarantees absence of common bias.","Original hypothetical exercise."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，全部輸入均非本工程操作參數：q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1；計算：joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical exercise; none of these inputs are operating parameters of this project: q1=0.0208 1; q2=0.03 1; calculation: joint_failure=q1*q2=0.000624 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b326-v16-39","title":"並聯備援與共同原因：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel redundancy and common cause: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「並聯備援與共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel redundancy and common cause” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"畫出供電、網路、冷卻和軟體版本的依賴圖，逐一驗證切換功能；以故障注入確認另一通道可承接完整需求。 列出兩通道共用的實體與軟體資源，分開注入單路故障及共因故障，核對失效狀態。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Map dependencies in power, networking, cooling and software versions, verify switching, and use fault injection to confirm the surviving channel can carry the full demand. List physical and software resources shared by both channels, inject individual and common-cause faults separately, and verify resulting failure states. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在獨立模型加入一個共同原因機率，對比結果，列出可用物理隔離與不同依賴路徑降低的風險。 再以本單元 q1 的對照值重算 joint_failure，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Add one common-cause probability to the independent model, compare the result, and identify risks reduced by physical separation and distinct dependencies. Also recalculate joint_failure for the alternative q1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","failure":"注意干擾：兩台設備接在同一配電盤可能被一次故障同時切斷；過載備援也可能在接手後立即失效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Two devices on one distribution board can be lost together, and an undersized backup can fail immediately after taking over. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"畫出供電、網路、冷卻和軟體版本的依賴圖，逐一驗證切換功能；以故障注入確認另一通道可承接完整需求。 列出兩通道共用的實體與軟體資源，分開注入單路故障及共因故障，核對失效狀態。","textEn":"Map dependencies in power, networking, cooling and software versions, verify switching, and use fault injection to confirm the surviving channel can carry the full demand. List physical and software resources shared by both channels, inject individual and common-cause faults separately, and verify resulting failure states.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在獨立模型加入一個共同原因機率，對比結果，列出可用物理隔離與不同依賴路徑降低的風險。 再以本單元 q1 的對照值重算 joint_failure，提交含單位、輸入來源和模型不適用條件的結果表。","textEn":"Add one common-cause probability to the independent model, compare the result, and identify risks reduced by physical separation and distinct dependencies. Also recalculate joint_failure for the alternative q1 value in this unit, submitting units, input provenance and conditions under which the model is inapplicable.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「並聯備援與共同原因」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel redundancy and common cause\"?","options":["畫出供電、網路、冷卻和軟體版本的依賴圖，逐一驗證切換功能；以故障注入確認另一通道可承接完整需求。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","風機已經啟動就能證明隧道每一處濃度同樣下降"],"optionsEn":["Map dependencies in power, networking, cooling and software versions, verify switching, and use fault injection to confirm the surviving channel can carry the full demand.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A running fan proves concentration falls equally at every point in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"畫出供電、網路、冷卻和軟體版本的依賴圖，逐一驗證切換功能；以故障注入確認另一通道可承接完整需求。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Map dependencies in power, networking, cooling and software versions, verify switching, and use fault injection to confirm the surviving channel can carry the full demand. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b326-v16-40","title":"並聯備援與共同原因：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel redundancy and common cause: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"prerequisiteIds":["b326-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「並聯備援與共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel redundancy and common cause” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩台設備接在同一配電盤可能被一次故障同時切斷；過載備援也可能在接手後立即失效。 兩個盒子不等於兩個獨立通道，須核對共用依賴。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Two devices on one distribution board can be lost together, and an undersized backup can fail immediately after taking over. Two boxes do not imply two independent channels; inspect their shared dependencies. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查環線控制備援是否仍受同一供電或機房事件影響。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Check whether ring-control redundancy remains exposed to one supply or equipment-room event.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要設備數量變成兩台失效機率就必定平方降低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling equipment count necessarily squares down the failure probability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b326-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩台設備接在同一配電盤可能被一次故障同時切斷；過載備援也可能在接手後立即失效。 兩個盒子不等於兩個獨立通道，須核對共用依賴。","textEn":"Two devices on one distribution board can be lost together, and an undersized backup can fail immediately after taking over. Two boxes do not imply two independent channels; inspect their shared dependencies.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]},{"id":"b326-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「並聯備援與共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel redundancy and common cause\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","兩台設備接在同一配電盤可能被一次故障同時切斷；過載備援也可能在接手後立即失效。","環狀線沒有終端折返就不必核對單圈時間與車組數"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Two devices on one distribution board can be lost together, and an undersized backup can fail immediately after taking over.","A circular line without terminal reversal need not check loop time against fleet size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"兩台設備接在同一配電盤可能被一次故障同時切斷；過載備援也可能在接手後立即失效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Two devices on one distribution board can be lost together, and an undersized backup can fail immediately after taking over. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-b326-history","v16s-b301-iec-rams-1","v16s-b301-iec-rams-2","v16s-b326-background"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b326-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b326-en.svg"}};
